(Disables NetBIOS over TCP)

wmic nicconfig where TcpipNetbiosOptions=0 call SetTcpipNetbios 2

Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_NetworkAdapterConfiguration -Filter "TcpipNetbiosOptions = 0" | Invoke-CimMethod -MethodName SetTcpipNetbios -Arguments @{TcpipNetbiosOptions = 2}

Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_NetworkAdapterConfiguration -Filter "IPEnabled = True" | Invoke-CimMethod -MethodName SetTcpipNetbios -Arguments @{TcpipNetbiosOptions = 2}

Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_NetworkAdapterConfiguration -Filter "IPEnabled = True" | Select-Object Description, TcpipNetbiosOptions

0: Default (Use NetBIOS setting from DHCP server)

1: Enable NetBIOS over TCP/IP

2: Disabled NetBIOS over TCP/IP

Get-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NetBT\Parameters\Interfaces\Tcpip_*' | Select-Object PSChildName, NetbiosOptions

Get-ChildItem -Path 'HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NetBT\Parameters\Interfaces' | ForEach-Object { Set-ItemProperty -Path $_.PSPath -Name NetbiosOptions -Value 2 }

Get-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NetBT\Parameters\Interfaces\Tcpip_*' | Select-Object PSChildName, NetbiosOptions

Restart-NetAdapter -Name "*"

Set-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NetBT\Parameters' -Name "NodeType" -Value 2 -Type DWord

Set-Service -Name "lmhosts" -StartupType Disabled
Stop-Service -Name "lmhosts" -Force











If you want to disable any protocol on the network – here is an example template:

Disable-NetAdapterBinding -Name "Ethernet" -ComponentID ms_implant


When you want to re-enable it:

Enable-NetAdapterBinding -Name "Ethernet" -ComponentID ms_implant


Disable "File and Printer Sharing for Microsoft Networks"

Disable-NetAdapterBinding -Name "Ethernet" -ComponentID ms_server




netsh int ipv4 show global


netsh int ipv6 show global


netsh interface ipv4 show interface "Ethernet"


netsh interface ipv6 show interface "Ethernet"


Command to disable ICMP Redirects in IPv4:

netsh interface ipv4 set global icmpredirects=disabled


Command to enable ICMP Redirects in IPv4:

netsh interface ipv4 set global icmpredirects=enabled


